From 2f705eaaef1b213bfee2dc92d2083bbcbb8163ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:50:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] resolve: a named import shadows the extern prelude in 2018+ use paths

async-compression 0.4.44 (tombi 1.8.4) lib.rs:161-163:

    pub use compression_core as core;
    pub use core::Level;

failed with "Unable to resolve `use` target ::"core-0_0_0"::Level".
rustc resolves the first segment of a use path in the module (items
and named imports) before the extern prelude, so `core` is
compression_core here. The local-shadow check added for colorgrad's
`mod core` only counted items, so the path went to libcore.

When the first segment names an extern-prelude crate, a named import of
that name in the same module now shadows it if it binds the type
namespace to something other than that crate (resolved on demand when
it comes later in the module, cycle-guarded). Value- and macro-only
imports (`use log::{log, info};`) and `use core::{self}` (same crate,
old route kept) don't count; globs are not consulted (rustc reports
a glob that differs from the extern prelude as ambiguous).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
